# Copy-only clang-tidy config — the type-aware companion to the regex lint.py.
#
# This C++ is memory-bound; the dominant cost is data movement / cache behavior,
# and an accidental by-value copy of a heavy type (Box, capd::IMap, Environment,
# IntervalVector, ...) is a silent regression a regex lint cannot see (a copy is
# semantic, not syntactic). These five built-in performance checks are exactly the
# copy-detection subset. Run them via ./copy_lint.sh (incremental, changed .cc vs.
# merge-base) — it adds --warnings-as-errors and the macOS -isysroot fixup.
#
# Findings are resolved by fixing (const& / move / drop a no-op std::move) or, when
# a copy is genuinely needed, justified inline with // NOLINT(performance-...) <why>
# — the native twin of lint.py's `// lint: allow`.
#
# No WarningsAsErrors here on purpose: editors/clangd surface these as plain
# warnings; the hard fail is the gate script's job.
Checks: >
  -*,
  performance-unnecessary-value-param,
  performance-for-range-copy,
  performance-unnecessary-copy-initialization,
  performance-move-const-arg,
  performance-implicit-conversion-in-loop
HeaderFilterRegex: 'src/dreal/.*'
